{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773077055,"nonce":"w5S5izkM0pS2DNjIffir/Arw03g=","title":"renameTab bypasses isDirty: project renames not auto-saved","message":"projectsStore renameTab uses useGraphStore.setState({...}) directly rather than going through a store action. This means isDirty is never set to true on rename, so the debounced auto-save does not fire.\n\nIf the user renames a project tab and closes the browser within 800ms (or before any content edit), the rename is lost.\n\nFix: call markDirty() (or an equivalent store action) inside renameTab after mutating graph.metadata.name.","files":null}]}